  <title>The log</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Help</gui><gui>View log</gui></guiseq> shows the log of this
  session: the messages and errors PyGtk Posting has printed since it started.
  When something goes wrong, the log is what to send to whoever looks after
  PyGtk Posting. The log is read again each time you click into the
  window.</p>

  <note><p>The log is only kept when PyGtk Posting is started with
  <cmd>run.sh</cmd> or from the installed program. Otherwise the window says
  the log file was not found.</p></note>

  <p>Every session's log is kept in <file>~/.config/posting/logs</file>,
  named by the date and time PyGtk Posting was started, so the log of a
  session that has ended can still be read there.</p>

</page>
